From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Bryan <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:24:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(core): write receipts name the fields the call changed

The research build's write receipts (usability/01) carried only each object's
identity and version, so a caller could not see from the answer what the write
changed. MWS-RES-4 asks for that, and the research build fell below it on
resources_create_or_update (3 write paths).

The default receipt now adds, under `changed`, each field the call changed with
its new value (null for a removed field): for an existing object, the fields that
differ between a read made just before the write and the API's answer; for a
created object, the fields the call sent. If the earlier read fails, the fields the
call sent are listed under `set` instead. Status and server-maintained metadata are
left out, strings are cut at 256 characters and at most 50 fields are listed.

`output: compact` keeps the identity-and-version receipt that the benchmark
measured; `output: full` still returns the whole objects. Applies to
resources_create_or_update, resources_patch and pods_run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
